    <!-- The xsd caps <summary> at 128 characters (type l10n-string). -->
    <summary>Team workspace for Nextcloud: messages, decisions, presence, projects, services. A self-hosted Microsoft Teams alternative.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[**Your users are asking for Microsoft Teams. Your auditor is asking who approved what, and where it is stored. TeamHub answers both from the Nextcloud you already run.**

A Nextcloud Team on its own is a membership list. TeamHub turns that list into a governed workspace: messages, decisions, presence, a timeline and projects on one page per team, beside the Talk conversation, team space, Calendar, Collective and Deck board that team already uses. Deck stays the source of truth for cards, Talk for conversations, Files for documents — TeamHub reads across them, writes your actions back to them, and records what happened.

**Control**
- Teams are created from templates and carry policy profiles — apps, modules and settings decided before anyone joins
- Gates are server-side, not interface-side: every controller method checks membership and role
- No side doors — a team made in Contacts, Collectives or `occ` is not a TeamHub team, and a TeamHub team cannot be deleted from Nextcloud's Teams page
- Bulk rollout from CSV, with a dry run that creates nothing until you confirm
- Restricted means hidden: an action a role may not perform is not rendered at all

**Evidence**
- Append-only per-team audit log — membership, files, shares, resources and configuration, with actor and before/after. Retention 7–3650 days. Exports as JSON
- Changes made outside TeamHub are pulled in hourly from Nextcloud's own activity and share tables
- ISO/IEC 27001:2022 control report — this instance's live state against the Annex A controls TeamHub can evidence, and the ones it cannot
- Decisions with no delete button; service requests sealed with a re-verifiable SHA-256 chain
- Code integrity checked against a SHA-256 manifest generated at build time

**Residency**
- Runs entirely inside your Nextcloud — no hosted version, no external service, no sub-processor to add to your register
- An instance with an active licence transmits nothing at all
]]></description>
